{
  "version": "M365-1.3 (2026-10-09)",
  "sources": {
    "verb_levels": "https://learn.microsoft.com/powershell/scripting/developer/cmdlet/approved-verbs-for-windows-powershell-commands (100 approved verbs, fetched 2026-09-15). Where, ForEach, Sort and Tee are not approved verbs but are the verbs of Where-Object, ForEach-Object, Sort-Object and Tee-Object, so they stay. The level is Microsoft's verb meaning read as tenant impact: Get/Find/Search/... read, Set/New/Add/... change, Remove/Clear/Uninstall delete. Import, Join, Request, Skip, Hide, Connect and Disconnect moved to CHANGES on 2026-10-09: Microsoft 365 modules use them for writes (Import-TransportRuleCollection, Request-SPOPersonalSite, Join-MgSiteContentTypeWithHubSite, Skip-MgDeviceManagementManagedDeviceActivationLock, Hide-MgChatForUser, Connect-Mailbox), and the sign-in cmdlets are an override. Unapproved verbs Exchange and Purview use: Delete (Delete-QuarantineMessage) deletes; Release, Rotate, Upgrade, Expedite, Cancel, Execute, Redirect, Retry, Clean change; Preview reads. Checked against the Graph SDK MgCommandMetadata.json (Microsoft.Graph.Authentication 2.41.1: the HTTP method of all 27,242 Graph cmdlets) and the Learn and PnP page of each cmdlet named here, fetched 2026-10-09.",
    "cmdlet_overrides": "Search-Mailbox and New-ComplianceSearchAction pages under https://learn.microsoft.com/powershell/module/exchange/ (fetched 2026-09-15)",
    "undo": "each docs URL, fetched 2026-09-15; the retention figures are quoted from those pages"
  },
  "verb_levels": {
    "READ-ONLY": ["Get", "Find", "Search", "Select", "Show", "Test", "Measure", "Compare", "Read", "Receive", "Resolve", "Trace", "Debug", "Ping", "Format", "Out", "Where", "ForEach", "Sort", "Group", "Split", "ConvertTo", "ConvertFrom", "Convert", "Export", "Write", "Tee", "Wait", "Watch", "Enter", "Exit", "Step", "Use", "Assert", "Confirm", "Checkpoint", "Expand", "Compress", "Save", "Push", "Pop", "Limit", "Preview"],
    "CHANGES": ["Set", "New", "Add", "Update", "Enable", "Disable", "Grant", "Revoke", "Move", "Rename", "Resize", "Restore", "Register", "Unregister", "Publish", "Unpublish", "Install", "Initialize", "Invoke", "Send", "Submit", "Sync", "Start", "Stop", "Restart", "Suspend", "Resume", "Lock", "Unlock", "Block", "Unblock", "Protect", "Unprotect", "Approve", "Deny", "Merge", "Copy", "Complete", "Undo", "Redo", "Repair", "Optimize", "Backup", "Mount", "Dismount", "Switch", "Edit", "Close", "Open", "Reset", "Deploy", "Build", "Import", "Join", "Request", "Skip", "Hide", "Connect", "Disconnect", "Release", "Rotate", "Upgrade", "Expedite", "Cancel", "Execute", "Redirect", "Retry", "Clean"],
    "DESTRUCTIVE": ["Remove", "Clear", "Uninstall", "Delete"]
  },
